What is OOP?

OOP (Object-Oriented Programming) is a way of writing programs using objects.

Instead of writing everything as functions, we create objects that contain:

Data (variables)
Actions (functions)

These are called attributes and methods.

Four Main Pillars of OOP==>

We'll learn these one by one.

1. Class
2. Object
3. Inheritance
4. Polymorphism
5. Encapsulation
6. Abstraction

